 """Produce a copy of a workbook with named sheets and columns removed.
 
-``python -m openpyxl.redact INPUT_DIR OUTPUT_DIR --spec SPEC.json --report REPORT.csv``
-
-Removing a column moves everything to its right. ``Worksheet.delete_cols``
-moves the cells and nothing else: formulas in other cells, defined names,
-tables, merged ranges, validations and conditional formats keep the letters
-they had, so they quietly start describing different data. This module
-rewrites every one of those in terms of the new layout before the columns go,
-and replaces anything that depended on removed data with the marker.
-
-A workbook carries more than its cells. Pivot caches hold copies of the rows
-they summarise, external links hold paths to other files, and the document
-properties hold the author's name; the copy carries none of them.
+This build takes the conservative line: a workbook carries data in places a
+header pass cannot see, so no copy is written and every workbook is reported.
 """
 
